skill: "runway-sensitivity-analysis"
sections[3]:
  - "# runway-sensitivity-analysis\n\nExtend the 13-week cash forecast into scenario runway bands with named cost levers, and synthesize the board financial deck outline from them. Use monthly before board cadence, when a hiring or spend decision lands, or whenever the base-case floor distance narrows below policy tolerance.\n\nOwner: role-cfo (pod-gna, executive). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[4]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"cashflow-13w.toon from treasury; opex plan opex-plan.toon; revenue forecast inputs; board deck policy board-deck-policy.toon\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/finance/runway-scenarios.toon with base|down|up bands, runway months per band, levers[] with trigger conditions; board-deck-outline.toon\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Load cashflow-13w.toon and confirm it reconciles with the latest settlement-recon and aging inputs; a stale forecast blocks the analysis and is reported as such.\n2. Define the scenario bands: base as-is, down (revenue misses and pipeline slips), up (plan beats); each band states its assumptions explicitly.\n3. Compute runway months per band with run_command: months until the liquidity floor is breached, not until zero cash - the floor is the operating constraint.\n4. Build the cost lever list: each lever names the spend block, the monthly saving, the time to effect and the trigger condition that pulls it; levers without a trigger are not levers, they are wishes.\n5. Order levers by cash impact per unit of organizational damage; state the order explicitly so the down case is a plan, not a panic list.\n6. Cross-check the down case against cap-table-scenarios.toon: if the down band breaches the floor before the next funding window, mark the funding dependency in the report.\n7. Synthesize board-deck-outline.toon per board-deck-policy.toon: the sections, the chart list with the artifact each chart reads from, and the one-page financial summary.\n8. Emit ask_question to role-cfo to review the outline before assembly; write runway-scenarios.toon with every assumption traceable to a source artifact.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\noutline to board pack; lever triggers registered with hiring and spend owners.\n"
